{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_bg6qtkpyz2fnxyrabmv3ccoyujcuhisn6crqbafthpta4ajulwya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Build succeeds with only warnings (unused imports in the original interface and unused helpers in test file). Let me summarize the work:\n\n## Summary\n\n### Phase 1: Translation\nI translated the C dictionary implementation in `c_src/src/dict.c` into idiomatic, safe Rust in `src/dict.rs`. Key implementation choices:\n\n- Replaced the C linked-list buckets with `Vec<DictElem>` per bucket for safe iteration/removal.\n- Replaced the C `va_list` variable arguments with byte slices (`&[u8]`) for keys.\n- Implemented hash, equality, padding logic to match C's exact semantics including:\n  - Sign-extension for signed types (e.g., `-1` → `u64::MAX`)\n  - Float-to-int conversion via signed path (matches GCC's `cvttss2si`/`cvttsd2si` behavior for negative floats)\n  - String hash uses `code = (code * 256 + signed_byte) % 1000000007`\n  - Reshape triggered when bucket size exceeds `mod_+1` (matches C's `size++ > mod` post-increment)\n- Pure safe Rust — no `unsafe`, no FFI, no `libc`.\n\n### Phase 2: Tests\nAdded 39 tests in `src/bin/test_dict.rs` covering every public API:\n- `dict_create`, `dict_new`, `dict_create_args` — constructor variants and padding behavior\n- `dict_get` — insertion, overwrite, zero-init slot, value lookup, returns-zeroed-slot\n- `dict_has` — present/absent keys including after remove\n- `dict_remove` — present, missing, then reinsert\n- `dict_len` — empty/non-empty/post-remove\n- `dict_key` — empty (returns None) and populated (returns 4*N bytes for I32)\n- `dict_serialize` — empty, I32→double, STR→i32 with exact byte counts and headers verified against C output\n- `dict_deserialize` — round-trip for both I32 and STR keys\n- `dict_get_hash` — exact ground-truth hashes from C for I32, U32, F64, Char (signed), and String types\n- `dict_reshape` — verifies capacity grows past `DEFAULT_MOD` and all values still retrievable after rehashing\n- `dict_destroy` — verifies count returns to zero\n\nAll expected values were obtained by compiling and running the C source against helpers, then asserting the exact same values in Rust. All 39 tests pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":241,"cache_read_input_tokens":82358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":241,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06855d30-ac13-4eaf-b027-415f0efbbd04","uuid":"c9b3e80d-5a1d-460d-841e-5c937a745331"}
